      "side": 1,
      "message": "This seems very suspicious. `nmad` is supposed to be equivalent to a `_mm256_fnmadd_ps`. Another way to write it would be `_mm256_fmadd_ps(-f, m, a)`. I don\u0027t have Loongarch docs, so I don\u0027t know what `__lasx_xvfnmadd_s` does, but negating `a` seems wrong unless your `fnmadd` is quite different from both Intel\u0027s and ARM\u0027s.\n\nHave you run the unit tests? Normally I would expect our CI to do it for us, but since we don\u0027t have Loongarch hardware available to us, you will need to do it yourself :)\n\nPlease try running: `out/Debug/dm -m SkRasterPipeline`\n\nAnd make sure all tests are actually passing.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 956,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 956,
        "endChar": 74
      },
      "revId": "3c54c66c2087710a20951a1ccf86af230eda2b84",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "02114943_1bc7c295",
        "filename": "src/opts/SkRasterPipeline_opts.h",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 956,
      "author": {
        "id": 21814
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-25T03:38:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Our fnmadd is indeed quite different from both Intel\u0027s and ARM\u0027s.\nThe operation of ```__lasx_xvfnmadd_s``` is:\n```\nfor i in range(4):\n    dst[i] \u003d -(f[i] * m[i] + a[i]); \n```\nIt\u0027s actually just negating the result of the vfmadd operation, so we use ```-a``` to get the same result.\n\nAnd we can make sure all the tests have been passed.",
      "parentUuid": "6459757a_4ef9d0cb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 956,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 956,
        "endChar": 74
      },
      "revId": "3c54c66c2087710a20951a1ccf86af230eda2b84",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e18b6ea3_32e04344",
        "filename": "src/opts/SkRasterPipeline_opts.h",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 956,
